<metadata><name>Cinnamon Butte and Wits End</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:303-4: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.236905" lon="-122.143683"><ele>1474.0</ele><name>Highway 138 parking (Cinnamon Butte Road)</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:cinnamon-butte-parking (OSM way 1214217619); confidence: high; pdf_page: 306; book_elev_ft: 4860; quote: The small trailhead parking area is on Highway 138, 3.7 miles north of the Diamond Lake Resort access road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.232100" lon="-122.115200"><ele>1691.1</ele><name>Road 4793 / 4793100 junction</name><desc>source: USFS road 4793000 meets 4793100 (shared vertex); confidence: high; pdf_page: 306; book_elev_ft: 5550; quote: At 1.7 miles turn left off the road onto a moderately steep, primitive road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.241062" lon="-122.109705"><ele>1956.7</ele><name>Cinnamon Butte lookout</name><desc>source: OSM peak node 357308066 (= end of USFS road 4793000); confidence: high; pdf_page: 305; book_elev_ft: 6417; quote: The distance to the fire lookout on Cinnamon Butte (6,417 feet) is 3.2 miles</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.232100" lon="-122.115200"><ele>1691.1</ele><name>Road 4793 / 4793100 junction</name><desc>source: back down the primitive road; confidence: high; pdf_page: 306; book_elev_ft: 5550</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.229730" lon="-122.068740"><ele>2039.2</ele><name>Road turns east and drops</name><desc>source: USFS road 4793100 vertex where it turns from north to east, 167 m south of the Wits End peak; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 307; quote: follow a road to where it turns east and drops. Remain on the ridge, leave the road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.230925" lon="-122.069996"><ele>2061.8</ele><name>Wits End</name><desc>source: OSM peak node 357318246; confidence: high; pdf_page: 307; book_elev_ft: 6782; quote: climb the ridge northward 200 yards for the best views</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.229730" lon="-122.068740"><ele>2039.2</ele><name>Road turns east and drops</name><desc>source: return; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 307</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.232100" lon="-122.115200"><ele>1691.1</ele><name>Road 4793 / 4793100 junction</name><desc>source: return; confidence: high; pdf_page: 306; book_elev_ft: 5550</desc></wpt>
